--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 225d9b1d2725f744893b380e958420b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: "Scene 7 \u2014 Resolution (The Argument) DIalogueSO"
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: 
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: Three districts. Three increasingly expensive systems. And downtown
      still flooded on my watch.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: We're aware. We take full responsibility for the technical failure.
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: Do you? Because from where I'm standing, this contract promised
      a solution, and what we got was a very well-funded delay.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: "With respect, Mayor \u2014 every device we deployed outperformed
      its predecessor. Detection speed, capacity, response time. We hit every technical
      benchmark we set ourselves."
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: Then explain the flood.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: The flood happened because thousands of people decided, on their
      own, to throw trash into the water anyway. That's not a hardware problem.
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: It's still a problem your system was supposed to solve.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: "No. It's a problem our system was supposed to manage. Those aren't
      the same thing, and I think that's where this contract went wrong from the
      start \u2014 not in the engineering, but in the expectation."
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (pointed) Careful, Mr. CEO. That sounds like you're blaming my
      citizens.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: 'I''m not blaming anyone. I''m naming what''s actually true: no
      interceptor, no AI camera, no smart block can out-scale a habit that thousands
      of people repeat every single day. We built the best prevention system we could.
      It slowed the damage. It didn''t stop the cause.'
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (a beat, quieter) ...You're saying the city built the safety net,
      and people walked past it anyway.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: I'm saying the safety net was never meant to replace the choice
      not to fall. We can catch what falls. We can't make people stop letting go.
      Every piece of trash in a waterway is a choice someone made, upstream, days
      before the water ever rose.
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (sitting down, some of the anger draining into something heavier)
      So what am I supposed to tell the residents of Downtown? That their flooded
      homes are a "behavioral issue"?
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: "No. Tell them the truth \u2014 that clogged drains and flooded
      streets aren't just infrastructure failures. They're the result of waste that
      never should have entered the water in the first place. And that no amount
      of funding can automate away someone's choice not to care."
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (long silence) ...So what would you have me do instead? Cancel
      the program?
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: "No. Keep it. It's still holding back real damage every single
      day \u2014 ask Riverside. But pair it with something we never budgeted for:
      the public has to become part of the system, not just something the system
      defends against. Education. Visibility. Consequences people actually see and
      understand, not just infrastructure they never think about until it fails."
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (a small, tired nod) ...That's not the kind of contract ArcoSteel
      can fulfill alone.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: "No. It never was. We can build the walls. We can't build the will
      behind them. That part was always going to be the city's \u2014 every resident,
      every district, every person who's ever stood over a drain with something in
      their hand and a choice to make."
  - characterName: Veronica
    dialogueLine: (standing, looking out at the city) Then maybe that's the real
      project. Not another device. A city that finally understands what its water
      is worth.
  - characterName: Mr. CEO
    dialogueLine: That's the only project that was ever going to actually work.
